WEBVTT


00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:06.820
The needle retaining bar also known as
a sponge bar or sponge presser bar on

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:11.490
knitting machines holds the needles
in place for proper Stitch formation.

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:15.480
Most metal bed machines
have this retaining bar.

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:21.900
A deteriorated or flattened sponge bar
is the cause of many problems that new

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.040
Knitters experience.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:28.130
Replacing the sponge bar is simple
and should be done regularly.

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:34.315
Now this photo is an exaggeration.

00:00:34.525 --> 00:00:38.595
But if your needles are sitting up
and they're not tight against the bed.

00:00:38.754 --> 00:00:41.375
It's time to replace your sponge bar.

00:00:42.155 --> 00:00:46.625
They are available online from many
retailers and they're relatively

00:00:46.625 --> 00:00:47.625
inexpensive.

00:00:49.175 --> 00:00:53.105
Many Knitters will remove their sponge bar
from the machine when they're not knitting

00:00:53.105 --> 00:00:54.705
for long periods of time.

00:00:55.660 --> 00:01:00.340
Some Knitters will rotate sponge bars
using one and let the other rest.

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:03.269
This may prolong the life of the bar.

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:09.710
But normal deterioration will flatten the
sponge and require replacing at some point

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:15.390
a flat and sponge Bart can cause
many many issues in your knitting.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:19.180
It can cause broken or bent needles.

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:21.620
Damage to your carriage.

00:01:22.964 --> 00:01:24.804
Skip stitches in patterning.

00:01:25.455 --> 00:01:29.985
Drop stitches and general
knitting problems.

00:01:32.244 --> 00:01:37.315
To replace your sponge bar first
remove the carriage from the machine.

00:01:38.685 --> 00:01:43.104
Be sure that all the needles are pushed
back into A or non-working position.

00:01:44.435 --> 00:01:47.945
Don't remove the sponge bar when the
needles are fully out or in holding

00:01:47.945 --> 00:01:49.285
position.

00:01:54.405 --> 00:02:00.040
Start by using a screwdriver or a sturdy
tool of some sort to push the end of that

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:02.260
bar to the inside of the Machine.

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:06.970
Push far enough so that you can
take hold of it at the other end.

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:12.190
Pull the bar firmly
and start to remove it.

00:02:13.715 --> 00:02:17.565
Now notice how the bar is positioned
in the machine before removing.

00:02:17.595 --> 00:02:18.475
It completely.

00:02:19.095 --> 00:02:23.465
Most commonly this sponge is
face down against the needles.

00:02:25.855 --> 00:02:31.005
Also notice as you're pulling it out how
the needles pop-up away from the bed.

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:38.700
To replace the bar user needle Pusher to
hold the needles down and replace the bar

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:39.620
on top of them.

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:44.850
Work your way slowly across the bed
until the bar is completely inserted.

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:51.220
Our knitting machines don't take a lot
of Maintenance that this is one thing you

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:52.810
can't ignore.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:54.400
Change your sponge bar.

